    "body": "Well, just inspected the git modules for a while,\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n$ time ~/Eric/MyPrograms/rust/starship/target/debug/starship prompt                                                                                   \r\n ERROR starship::modules::git_status > Status Start: SystemTime { tv_sec: 1572264031, tv_nsec: 932834367 }                                            \r\n ERROR starship::modules::git_status > After ahead behind: Ok(571.217µs)                                                                              \r\n ERROR starship::modules::git_status > After stash parse: Ok(686.442µs)                                                                               \r\n ERROR starship::modules::git_status > After repo status: Ok(597.710638ms)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt seems that `repository.statuses()` consumes a lot of time. This function is not an iteration and async functions have to be used to set a timeout to it.",
