    "created_at": "2021-05-02T08:34:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-02T08:34:38Z",
    "body": "Similar to #940 I am going to close this issue since we have switched to calling git and parsing the output rather than using libgit2. As mentioned in the other issue this should both be faster for larger repos and will respect the `command_timeout` setting so starship won't hang while trying to get the status of the repo. While this isn't a perfect solution it should hopefully be sufficient until we can introduce a cache, async rendering, a daemon or some combination of all three. ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
